  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"[A] collaborative work and refers to how we all enter the system of education as an institution and as a process. The book is constructed from stories solicited by Thomas Rose and Bryant Griffith as part of a larger project titled 'School stories'. The images, editing, constructed text and layouts are by Thomas Rose, as is the audio editing and sound design. The CD graphics are by Mary Rose, with final mastering and production of the CDs by PowerHouse Studios of Minneapolis. Wendy Fernstrum was the copy editor. Wilber Schilling was responsible for the design of the book's overall format. The edition was letterpress printed and bound at Indulgence Press in Minneapolis in the spring of 2003. The photographic images were printed on an Epson 2000 photo stylus inkjet printer onto Hahnemühle Photo Rag Duo, mould-made paper. The text and line art were printed from photopolymer plates on a Vandercook SP-20 cylinder press. The text is excerpted from stories by: Ken Aper, William Clark, Larry Connolly, Marc Cutright, Arthur C. Danto, David Goldes, Bryant Griffith, John Killacky, George Laboucane, Jim Melchert, Tim Miller, Clarence Morgan, Kellen Pen, Archi Rand, Robert Reford, Thomas Rose, Thomas Leslie Rose, Richard Sigmund, Paul Vangelisti, Bob Williamson"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in a bookboard chemise and slipcase, both covered in red and black cloth. The chemise has black paper pockets attached to the inside of each board, holding audio discs A and B. Laid in the chemise is a folding book structure attached to front, back, and middle boards. Pages are printed with color illustrations, photographs, and text. The colophon is attached to the back side of the middle board.</subfield>
  </datafield>
